rd scheduling area is to sweep; anomalies matter. But the change list doesn't include scheduler. Still, we should check consistency of scheduling: e.g., set due date dialog (changed) and intervals.\n\nLet me not modify deck options. Back out and go to Card browser to test set due date.\n\nActually wait: the deck options \"used by 3 decks\". Let me check if this is a real inconsistency. Current decks: French, Spanish. Preset \"Default\" used by 2 decks. It says 3. This could be a stale count from our subdeck create/delete? That seems unlikely to persist. Let me later check again in a fresh state. Perhaps there are 3 decks because the backend still counts the deleted subdeck? Hmm, we deleted \"Renamed\" via UI; the deck should be gone.\n\nLet me press back and check deck list once more (it showed 2). Then revisit deck options later to see if count still 3. Actually could be \"3 decks\" includes \"Default\" deck? Anki has an implicit \"Default\" deck? In AnkiDroid, creating a subdeck under Spanish with preset... Hmm.\n\nLet me continue: back to deck overview, back to deck list, then Card browser."}
