{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: switching note type to Cloze and leaving via back does not persist; reopening shows Basic. This is likely the intended bug: \"a switch of note model is now stored to the collection straight away\" — should persist, but doesn't.\n\nBut wait: Maybe the note type is only stored when the note is added (saved), and \"stored straight away\" means something else: when you switch the model in the Add note screen, the fields/content may be reset... Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe persistence happens only if there's no note content? No, we had empty.\n\nActually, think about AnkiDroid: In Add note, the note type and deck pickers on reopen are remembered from the collection config `lastNoteType`/`lastDeckId`, which is written when the note is added (on save). The change \"a switch of note model is now stored to the collection straight away\" might mean when the user changes the picker, the value is immediately written to the collection rather than only after adding a note. Our test suggests it's not.\n\nBut careful: maybe pressing BACK with empty fields returns to browser and the Add note screen is recreated from the collection config; if persistence happened, it would show Cloze. It shows Basic → bug likely.\n\nHowever, maybe the app saves note type only when a note is saved, and the phrase means \"on switching, the model choice for the 'new note' is saved into collection (rather than only local state)\". Hmm.\n\nLet me test the deck picker too: change Deck from Spanish to French, back out, reopen: does deck persist? If deck persists but model doesn't, that's inconsistent and confirms bug. Let's test.\n\nCurrently Add screen Type Basic, Deck Spanish. Tap Deck Spanish and choose French."}
