{"type": "thinking", "text": "Deck now French. Back out and reopen, check whether Deck persists as French while Type stays Basic.\n\nBut note: it's possible deck persistence is only stored when note is added. Let's test by adding a note in French with model Basic, then reopen and see default deck = French & type = Basic.\n\nActually to isolate model switch persistence, I should add a note with the switched model, which likely saves model as last-used. Hmm. The change says switch is stored immediately — but maybe the actual implementation stores the \"selected note type\" only when switching to a different note type while editing an *existing* note? Let's parse \"Add note pickers: a switch of note model is now stored to the collection straight away.\" Add note pickers = the pickers on the Add Note screen. A switch of note model (i.e., choosing a different model in the type spinner) is now stored to the collection straight away (so next time Add Note opens, it remembers the model). Our test: not remembered. Strong candidate bug.\n\nBut wait — there's a subtlety: when you back out of Add Note with unsaved content, AnkiDroid may discard the pending note and reset to defaults stored at last *save*. If the switch were stored immediately, it'd be remembered. It wasn't. So bug likely.\n\nHowever, maybe the persistence happens when the Add screen is exited via \"Navigate up\" (same as back) — we did that.\n\nLet me test deck persistence now: back out, reopen. If Deck is Spanish again, then neither persisted. If Deck is French, deck persisted but type didn't → inconsistency.\n\nActually the deck picker changed selected deck; AnkiDroid typically remembers last deck even after cancel? Let's see."}
