{"type": "thinking", "text": "Developer could not reproduce. Hmm. Maybe the persistence requires a different route/handling. Let me reconsider. Maybe the \"stored straight away\" means the switch is stored to the collection only when you *switch to a model while there is already content*? No.\n\nOr maybe the developer tested by selecting a model and then re-opening the Add screen from the **deck list FAB** (not browser toolbar). The AddNoteActivity might persist the model under a key used only when launching from deck list. Or vice versa: my route (browser's Add) might be a different activity path that resets.\n\nBut the note type is stored in the collection config; opening from any route should show it. Unless the saved value is read only in `AddNoteActivity`'s deck list path and not browser path... Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the intended persistence is across app restarts: The Add note screen defaults are loaded from the collection config which is saved at a later point? We left and reopened the same activity; if the collection config had been updated, it should show.\n\nWait — maybe the issue is my switch got reverted because I pressed back and AnkiDroid *discarded* the pending note including the model change (by design). The change note says \"a switch of note model is now stored to the collection straight away\" — perhaps this means when you switch the model in the picker, the *previously used model's note content* is stored? Hmm no.\n\nLet me think about what feature could be intended differently: In AnkiDroid, the Add Note screen has \"note type\" picker. There's a known behavior: when you change the note type, AnkiDroid will remember the note type for the *next note you add in the same session*? And the \"stored to the collection straight away\" means the change is saved even if you don't add the note, so the next Add Note opens with that model. That's what I tested. Developer says cannot reproduce. Maybe the test environment differs: perhaps you must switch model in Add note then rotate the device? Hmm.\n\nMaybe my press of BACK while keyboard is open discarded the change? In the last repro, back exited directly to browser, then Add showed Basic. Should count.\n\nLet me try a different approach: switch model to Cloze, then navigate away not via back but via drawer->Decks, then reopen Add from deck list FAB. Maybe the browser Add path resets, but collection config persisted.\n\nAlso, maybe the model switch is persisted only when switching *from a model with content* because the save only happens in `onNoteTypeSelected` after the editor is flushed. Since fields were empty, maybe no flush/save occurred. Hmm, but storing the model shouldn't depend on content.\n\nLet me test: type something in Front, switch model to \"Basic (and reversed card)\", note the confirm dialog (it may ask to discard?), then exit and reopen. If there's a dialog asking to discard, choose keep/discard? Let's see.\n\nActually, another thought: the \"Add note pickers\" might refer to the **deck picker and model picker in the Add note screen accessed from the deck list FAB**, and the persistence is that picking a model stores it as the default for *new notes added within the deck options*... I'm overanalyzing.\n\nLet me test via deck-list FAB route: exit browser to deck list, tap FAB \"+\", switch model to Cloze, back, reopen via FAB, check. Maybe that works (developer likely used this route)."}
