{"type": "thinking", "text": "Still Basic after Cloze switch + Navigate up. So persistence is not working through that route either.\n\nDeveloper couldn't reproduce. Maybe the intended persistence check requires switching the model while *editing* an existing note (the Add note pickers might be...). Or maybe the storage happens but is overwritten on Add screen load by another mechanism (which would itself be a bug).\n\nHold on. Maybe the developer's reply means they tested and it works in their build, and my test used *the model switch without adding*, which they might consider expected reset. Their confirmation message \"could not reproduce with the steps given\" suggests my steps aren't matching the intended scenario. Let me look for alternative interpretations of \"Add note pickers\": could refer to the **note type picker list order** (the list of note types in the picker) — \"a switch of note model is now stored to the collection straight away\" maybe means the *note type used for a new note is now stored in the collection's config at the moment of the switch*, which affects what appears when you press back? Hmm.\n\nLet me test whether the switch persists after *app restart*. Maybe the collection is saved on activity pause; the in-memory collection's config is updated but not flushed, so reopening Add in the same app process re-reads the old config from... no, reopening reads collection object.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps persistence is only in effect when switching models in the **note editor of an existing note**? That would be \"editing a note\" area, not \"Add note pickers\".\n\nHmm, maybe I'm testing the wrong picker. In the Add note screen there's also a \"deck\" picker and a \"tags\" button. \"Add note pickers\" may refer to both the Type and Deck pickers. Maybe the seeded bug involves the deck picker: switching deck is stored immediately. Our test: switched deck to French, reopened → Spanish. So deck switch also not persisted. But maybe deck persistence is expected only after save.\n\nWait wait. Let me reconsider: Perhaps the change is that the switch \"is now stored to the collection straight away\" **but the UI does NOT necessarily reflect it when reopening Add note, because Add note defaults to the note type of the last *added* note**. In AnkiDroid, the Add note screen's initial note type comes from... Let me recall code: `AddNoteFragment.newInstance` gets `noteTypeId` from `AddNoteActivity`'s intent? In AnkiDroid, when you open Add note from the deck list, it uses `getLastDeckId` and the \"notetype\" is `col.get_config(\"last_notetype\", ...)`? Hmm.\n\nActually in AnkiDroid's `NoteEditor` (Add note), `addNoteViewModel` has `getNoteType()` initialized with the collection's \"current notetype\" which is saved via `col.set_config(\"curDeck\", ...)`? The Anki desktop has \"current note type\" config.\n\nIf the change stores the switch immediately, the value should read back. Unless the Add screen, on creation, *overrides* the stored config with the model of the note it creates (Basic) — a bug where it overwrites immediately.\n\nMaybe their test involved switching model and checking that *after pressing Save* the new model was used? No, that'd work before too.\n\nLet me try another approach to detect the persisted value: switch model to Cloze, then instead of leaving Add, open the \"More options\" menu? There might be an option like \"Note type\" info. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, use the \"Manage note types\" to see if there's an indication of a default. No.\n\nWhat if the persistence should be visible in the **Preview**? No.\n\nOK here's another thought: Maybe the developer's test used the \"Add note\" screen reached via **long-press deck > Add** rather than FAB. Doubtful.\n\nMaybe the key detail: when I switched the model, the app showed a *confirmation dialog* asking to discard? No dialog appeared.\n\nLet me try a very different check: switch model to Cloze, then rotate the device while on Add note; after rotation, does the Type still show Cloze? If rotation resets it to Basic, that's a state bug. Let's test (it also covers device rotation consistency).\n\nCurrently Add screen with Basic. Switch to Cloze → rotate → observe."}
