{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now the \"all\" Future Due chart: x-axis labels 0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8, 1 (fractional!) while y-axis left 0..2 and right 0..4. The chart shows a large light-green filled area with a curve; this is a cumulative line chart? For \"all\" the x-axis is 0..1?? That seems wrong. Actually hmm: In Anki's Future Due graph, the x-axis is days; \"all\" should extend to the maximum due date. The largest due date in our collection: agua/comer due tomorrow (day 1), plus... hmm, but learning cards due today. Actually all future due dates span 0..1 day, so the \"all\" chart x-axis might be 0..1 (days)! Labels 0,0.2,0.4,0.6,0.8,1 = days 0..1. That makes sense! Because all due dates are within 0-1 day. And the chart shows a cumulative curve reaching 4 reviews at day 1 (right axis 4). The green area fills under the cumulative curve. So it's plausible: x-axis is days (0 to 1). Good — not a bug. The area is a cumulative count, not bars. OK.\n\nInteresting: chart uses left axis cards (max 2) and right axis reviews (max 4). The green area's height at x=1: left ~2? right 3? Hmm at x=1 the filled area top is around left-axis ~1.6 / right-axis ~3.6. The curve ends at ~3.6? But total 4 reviews. Hmm, the y-axis right labels 0,1,2,3,4. The curve at x≈1 approaches ~3.8-4. And left axis 0..2: filled area top at x=1 is near left 1.9 (right 3.9). Hmm plausible cumulative = 4 at x=1.\n\nBut wait: the filled green area at x=0 starts at y≈0? Actually at x=0 the top of filled area is ~0? The image shows filled region top-left at y≈0.5? Hard.\n\nOK this is the backend renderer's output; seems functional. Need to find the planted bug though. Options:\n- The chart may be \"cards\" vs \"reviews\" mismatch: bars/areas should represent the number of cards due each day; total 4 reviews but 4 cards? Consistent.\n- The \"Average\" for \"all\" changed to 4 reviews/day — hmm is that expected? In AnkiDroid, Future Due \"Average\" = reviews/day over the graph period; for \"all\" the period = days until last due? Average 4/day because 1 day span. Plausible.\n\nLet me test the \"1 year\" and check consistency. Also test \"last 12 months\" vs \"all history\" for Reviews: days studied etc.\n\nMaybe the planted bug is in a *specific* chart, e.g., the Calendar heatmap isn't rendering (all grey cells and one blue cell) — but NO DATA overlay suggests maybe. In the screenshot, Calendar shows 2026 grid with all cells light grey and one dark cell at bottom right. That's the standard heatmap (light grey = no reviews). Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug is the \"Save PDF\" button producing a broken PDF? Hard to verify.\n\nMaybe the bug is that charts show cumulative areas instead of bars — but that's the renderer's design.\n\nLet me compare deck stats vs collection stats for consistency: collection Card Counts total 8; deck Spanish total 5; French 3 new. Looks right.\n\nCheck the \"collection\"/\"deck\" switch: when I chose collection, the search box cleared (now shows \"Search\" placeholder). The deck name in toolbar still \"Spanish\" though mode is collection. Fine.\n\nHmm, one suspicious thing: When I selected \"collection\", the Future Due \"Today\" section still said \"Studied 4 cards\" (same). Fine.\n\nLet me switch back to \"deck\" mode and check its search text becomes deck:current. Also test switching to French via the deck dropdown and verify counts (French 3 new, reviews 0). Then test \"all history\" range.\n\nActually, wait. A more promising check: the deck dropdown (TextView \"Spanish\" with a ▾). Tapping it should list decks. Let me tap element 1."}
