atistics screen (charts backend). The toolbar/radio isn't changed. Hmm, but it's still an area to sweep: \"check that what each screen shows agrees with the data\". The radio inconsistency is a minor state bug. However, is it actually inconsistent? Let me think: In AnkiDroid 2.16 stats, the radio \"deck\"/\"collection\" and search field co-exist: selecting \"collection\" sets search to \"\" (all collection); choosing a deck from the top selector sets search to deck:\"French\" and the radio switches to \"deck\". The radio being \"collection\" while search = deck:\"French\" is contradictory but maybe the radio only reflects the last mode used... Hmm.\n\nWait, earlier sequence: I selected \"collection\" radio; search cleared; then I opened the deck selector and picked French. The deck selector probably should set the radio to deck. It didn't. This might be a genuine bug but outside the changed areas (the stats screen toolbar). Actually, hold on: The radio buttons might not be radio-grouped as expected. When I tap \"collection\", does \"deck\" radio uncheck? Yes, it did (deck unchecked). When I picked French, neither radio changed. So UI shows collection active while query is French. I'd consider reporting this as wrong_value/consistency in stats screen. But is it \"a bug that remains\" in a changed area? The stats screen is one of the sweep areas. The charts are changed, but the screen as a whole is in scope.\n\nHmm, but the sweep says test areas: study statistics screen. Yes, this counts.\n\nBut before reporting, let me check if the radio state actually reflects the query behavior: Does the screen show French stats (no cards studied today) or collection (4 studied)? It shows \"No cards have been studied today\", so French. So radio is wrong.\n\nAlso note the Future Due for French: no data because new cards only. But wait — the \"Future Due\" chart title says \"The number of reviews due in the future.\" If French has 3 new cards due today, the future due graph in Anki does not include new cards, so no data. OK.\n\nHmm, is it possible the search \"deck:\\\"French\\\"\" with collection radio is intentional: the radio \"collection\" is a saved search \"collection\" and the text field is editable; the radio just chooses between two presets. When you pick a deck, both apply? The rendering uses the search field. The radio might be a separate toggle that no longer matches. In AnkiDroid's actual UI, the radio group and search box are synchronized: typing in the search box unchecks both? I recall in AnkiDroid Statistics, there's a \"deck\" / \"collection\" toggle and a search bar; selecting deck shows deck:current, collection shows empty search. If you then edit the search text, radio may stay as is. Maybe acceptable.\n\nGiven uncertainty, maybe better to keep looking for a chart-specific bug.\n\nLet me compare charts across modes more carefully. E.g., in French deck, Card Counts should be New 3 (100%). Scroll down. Also \"Today\" card entirely missing for French (screenshot top begins with Future Due — the \"Today\" section is missing when no reviews? In the screenshot, after the toolbar there's Future Due directly; the elements included \"Today\" and \"No cards have been studied today.\" earlier though. In screenshot I don't see Today section at top; it starts with Future Due. Hmm — the earlier elements list showed TextView \"Today\" at y=254 and \"No cards have been studied today.\" at y=321, then Future Due at 499. In the screenshot, at y=254... the screenshot top shows \"Future Due\" card starting ~y=360? Actually the screenshot: top toolbar, then Future Due card at ~y=370. There's no \"Today\" section visible! Wait the screenshot is 1080x2400; the toolbar ~0-300; Future Due card title at ~480. So Today's section is missing visually even though elements said \"Today\". Hmm, maybe the screenshot was taken after a scroll offset (the content scrolled up slightly). The scroll position may have shifted. The \"Today\" section could be above the visible area. The elements y=254 for Today suggests it's at the very top area hidden under the toolbar. So can't conclude.\n\nLet me scroll to top for French."}
