o a different deck while the title remains. The user sees inconsistent data. I could report it. But I worry the developer might reject as \"expected: the deck:* search term is independent of title\". Hmm.\n\nLet me look for a stronger, more clearly wrong stats issue. Let me revisit the Future Due chart \"all\" for Spanish: the chart's x-axis was 0..1 with labels 0,0.2,... and y axes 0..2/0..4. Hmm.\n\nActually, wait. There's a real red flag: In the Future Due chart for \"1 month\" (Spanish), x-axis was 0..30 and the bars were at days 0 and 1. Total 4 reviews. The chart's left y-axis 0..2 and right 0..4. In Anki's Future Due chart, the right axis represents \"reviews\" and left \"cards\"? For 4 reviews due across 2 days, the max daily is 2, so left max 2; total reviews 4 → right max 4. But wait, the *right* axis should show cumulative reviews? Hmm, actually I now recall the Anki desktop Future Due graph has only one y-axis (number of reviews). But the AnkiDroid native FutureDueChart had two y-axes: left \"cards\" and right \"reviews\"? Hmm, I don't think AnkiDroid has dual-axis Future Due. Let me recall the AnkiDroid source: `FutureDueChart` extends `ChartView`, draws bars for `mDue` (cards) and a line for `mCumulative`? Hmm, maybe.\n\nActually yes! Anki's Future Due graph shows *bars* = cards due per day and a *line* = cumulative percentage? No wait, that's \"Reviews\" cumulative.\n\nLet me look at the screenshot of Spanish 1-month Future Due again: it showed only green bars, no line visible. Whatever.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the planted bug is that the Future Due chart shows \"Reviews\" total 4 while the correct number is 5? Hmm no.\n\nLet me try a different approach: inspect the \"collection\" + \"all history\" stats and see if the Today section and chart numbers disagree. With all history, days studied maybe differs.\n\nAlso there's a \"Time\" checkbox under Reviews: tapping it shows time spent instead of counts. Test it works and label/axis changes.\n\nLet me sc