{"type": "thinking", "text": "I'm far from Reviews. Let me use the deck dropdown to switch to collection? Not needed.\n\nInstead of hunting chart bugs with this data (which all checks out), let me consider that the planted stats bug might be visible in the \"Future Due\" chart x-axis/axis values or the bar rendering. Let me look at the 1-month Future Due chart closely with a screenshot and compare the bar positions with expected: bar at day 0 (today) height 2 and day 1 (tomorrow) height 2. In the first screenshot, there appeared to be a single green bar at the very left with width ~1.5 days. Let me re-examine by scrolling to Future Due and taking screenshot at 1 month.\n\nAlso: the Future Due chart's left axis max 2 and right axis max 4 — but the chart in AnkiDroid originally: the bars represent \"cards due\" per day using the left axis; the line represents \"cumulative reviews\" using right? In the 1-month screenshot, I only saw bars, no line. Hmm.\n\nLet me take a fresh screenshot of Future Due 1 month in collection mode with the deck picker correctly showing. Use radio \"collection\" then scroll to Future Due. Then analyze bars.\n\nActually, let me think about the \"all\" Future Due chart again: The area chart was green and filled with a curve. That's the *cumulative* view. For 1 month, it showed bars (green) because there were two days of data. Hmm, actually the 1-month chart might also be cumulative area but with only a thin sliver at the left? No, the screenshot showed a green vertical bar from y=0 to 2 at x≈0-1 and nothing else; that's a bar chart.\n\nWait, the \"all\" chart x-axis 0..1 over 1 day and a filled area — maybe it's a \"line chart\" because the number of bars would be 1? Inconsistent? Hmm, maybe not.\n\nLet me compare with AnkiDroid upstream: The native `FutureDueChart` draws bars (one per day) plus a cumulative line overlay. The backend renderer (Anki's graphs.py `future_due`) draws bars for cards due per day and a cumulative line on the right axis? Actually in Anki desktop, the Future Due graph shows bars for *cards* and a line for *reviews*? Hmm.\n\nGiven the \"all\" chart shows a *filled area under a curve*, that resembles a cumulative distribution, not bars. With x-axis 0..1 day, the curve rises from 0 to 4 as day progresses; the fill green. Actually Anki's backend Future Due chart is a *bar chart* (it uses `bar` for cards due) — not an area. Hmm, but maybe the renderer returns an image with both bars and a cumulative line. In our 1-month chart, the green \"bar\" at x≈0-1 was tall and solid, no line.\n\nI can't reliably judge renderer correctness without reference. Let me instead check the exact numbers with text; a planted bug may be in the *summary text* or in a chart's data. The summary texts looked consistent.\n\nNew idea: The task hint \"charts are now built by the backend statistics renderer instead of native views\" might mean the seeded bug is that **some chart is missing/crashes** or **chart doesn't load for certain stats** (e.g., \"Card Counts\" pie legend colors mismatched). Another typical bug: the chart's \"NO DATA\" shown even when data exists (we saw NO DATA text nodes but they're hidden behind the chart; in the French deck the NO DATA was visible because there truly was no data).\n\nWait — in the French Future Due with \"all\" selected, NO DATA was visible. Is that correct? French has 3 new cards; future due excludes new cards → no data. OK.\n\nBut hmm, what about the \"Card Counts\" in French: should show 3 new. Let me scroll down to check. Also \"Reviews\" NO DATA correct.\n\nAnother typical bug: the charts don't redraw when the timescale button is tapped (stale chart) — e.g., choosing \"3 months\" changes x-axis labels (we saw it did), so redraw works.\n\nMaybe the planted bug is in the *deck statistics title* (French) vs data (Spanish) — that's not charts though.\n\nLet me look at the \"Separate suspended/buried cards\" checkbox: toggle it and see if legend changes (all 0 anyway). Not informative.\n\nThe \"Retention\" Young/Mature/All radios: changing should alter table; all N/A. Not informative.\n\nThe \"Hourly Breakdown\" time range buttons: 1 month / 3 months / 1 year; chart with 4 reviews at hour 11 in all. Success rate axis 0-100%: the bar height used left axis (4) not percentage. If the chart's primary series is count, fine; success rate line may be a dot at 100% for hour 11; I didn't see a marker. Hmm.\n\nI wonder if the seeded bug is that the Hourly Breakdown uses counts instead of percentages for the bars (since the right axis is %). But the chart could legitimately show counts as bars and % as a line.\n\nLet me try to find the actual AnkiDroid implementation. In AnkiDroid native `HourlyBreakdownChart`:\n- It plots a bar chart of review counts (left axis) and a line of success rate (right axis)?\nI recall the AnkiDroid \"Hourly Breakdown\" graph shows bars (reviews) and a line (success rate). Let me check the screenshot: there was a single blue bar, no line visible. If a line should be drawn at 100% across hour 11, it might be a single point (invisible). OK.\n\nMaybe the best use of time: test other areas (deck management create deck, card scheduling via study, editing) and revisit stats later with a fresh session. The stats issue (header vs data) could be reported if reproducible cleanly. Let me first check if the deck-title/data mismatch reproduces from a clean path:\n1. Open Statistics from deck list (Spanish) -> header Spanish, search deck:current, data Spanish.\n2. Tap \"collection\" -> search empty, data collection.\n3. Pick French from dropdown -> header French, search deck:\"French\", data French.\n4. Tap \"deck\" -> search deck:current, header French, data ??? (Spanish).\n\nIf step 4 shows Spanish data with header French, it's a clear inconsistency. Let me do it carefully and observe. To make the difference obvious: French card counts total 3; Spanish 5.\n\nCurrently we're in a weird state (header French, search deck:current, data Spanish). Let me navigate back and reopen Stats from the drawer (fresh) to test cleanly.\n\nPress back to browser, then drawer -> Statistics."}
