{"type": "thinking", "text": "comer: interval 1 day, ease 250%. So both cards have 1-day intervals.\n\nReview Intervals chart with \"95%\": bars representing intervals; only interval 1 day. The blue area from 1 to 2 in the chart would be wrong if it's a bar chart. But maybe the x-axis scaling is not days but something else. Hmm.\n\nLet me analyze the chart rendering more precisely by taking a screenshot and looking at pixel positions. Actually, I can reason: The chart's x-axis labels 1, 1.2, 1.4 ... 3 — for a bar chart with intervals at 1, the bar would be placed at x=1 with some width. In the screenshot, the blue area starts at the left edge (x=1) and extends to about x=2 (the middle), height 2. So the \"bar\" is 1 unit wide. In AnkiDroid's native ReviewIntervalsChart, bars are drawn with a width of 1 day (barChart style), so a bar at 1 day spanning from 1.0 to 2.0 is expected! And the 95% line is at x=2 (the right edge of the bar)? Hmm, the median line at 1? The chart shows a lighter diagonal line inside the blue area (bar) — probably the cumulative line.\n\nActually, wait: the blue area extends from x=1 to x=2 with height 2 — that's exactly a bar of width 1 for interval 1 day, 2 cards. The gray area from x=2 to x=3 (height rising) might be the 95th-percentile region? Hmm, the gray shape's top edge rises from y≈1.6 at x=2 to y=2 at x=3 — odd.\n\nHmm, but maybe that's actually a *cumulative distribution* line over the bars. Anyway, bar chart interpretation fits: x=1 bar with width 1, height 2 = 2 cards at 1 day. The 95% cutoff marker at x=2 = 100%? Since 95% percentile of intervals [1,1] = 1, the cutoff line should be at x=1.5 or 2? With bar width 1, the 95% cumulative is reached within the bar at x=1... \n\nI can't resolve. The chart looks plausible enough.\n\nLet me now think about what to do: time is limited (we've used many steps). Remaining areas to cover:\n- Deck management: create deck via FAB (not yet tested), rename done, delete done, nested deck found bug. Also \"Create filtered deck\" maybe.\n- Adding/editing notes: add done, edit done, empty validation, note type switching (reported/rejected). Also tags, deck change on add, cancel/discard. Should test more.\n- Card scheduling: study Good/Easy, set due date day/range, card info. Also \"Again/Hard/Easy\" buttons and counts, undo? AnkiDroid study has undo via deck list menu. Also \"Reset progress\"/\"Grade now\". Maybe enough.\n- Stats: charts checked, found possible inconsistency.\n\nWe haven't tested deck creation via FAB, which is core deck management. Let's do that now. Also \"Change deck\" for a note.\n\nLet me go back to deck list. Press back from card info -> browser; back -> deck list. Then FAB → Create deck. Test empty name, valid name, cancel, persistence, delete."}
