{"type": "thinking", "text": "Agua restored to due 2026-11-15; interval likely 1 day. Good enough.\n\nNow, remaining tests:\n- Deck management: deck options (we looked at), rename, create, delete, filtered deck, undo. Done.\n- Adding/editing notes: add, edit, tags, note type switch (reported/rejected), deck picker, empty validation, save/cancel, delete. Also \"Change deck\" maybe test. We can test change deck on a temp note? Skip.\n- Card scheduling: study Good/Again/Easy, set due date, interval. Done. Could test \"Reset progress\" but not necessary.\n- Statistics: charts across ranges/deck/collection. Found possible UI inconsistency (radio/header). Also need to test the deck name dropdown consistency: statistics search \"deck:current\" vs header French.\n\nI should decide whether to report the statistics inconsistency. Let me test it once more in a clean, minimal sequence and see if it's really a bug worth reporting:\n\n1. From deck list (Spanish selected), open Statistics: header Spanish, deck radio checked, search deck:current, data Spanish.\n2. Change deck via header dropdown to French: header French, search deck:\"French\", but collection radio remains checked (should be deck?).\n3. Tap deck radio: header French, search deck:current, data Spanish (studied 4 cards / card count 5).\n\nData Spanish with header French is definitely user-visible inconsistency. But wait — maybe \"deck:current\" is defined as the deck from which Statistics was opened (Spanish), and the header is French because the user picked French; the radio \"deck\" might mean \"search deck:current\" which is documented to refer to the *currently selected deck in the deck list* (Spanish). In that case the header showing French is a leftover bug or by design? The dropdown title \"French\" indicates the statistics target deck; when the query is deck:current, the \"current\" should be the stats target (French). Right.\n\nHmm, but the \"deck:current\" search term in Anki is defined as \"the currently selected deck\" — inside the statistics screen, the search field is free text; \"current\" likely refers to the deck used by the stats screen (passed in intent). If the screen allows switching decks via the picker, it should update that.\n\nIs this worth a report? It's a consistency/navigation bug in the stats area. The instructions say to sweep statistics screen; finding this is legit. But will the developer confirm? Unknown. The fact that the radio doesn't update when picking a deck is also part of it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the backend stats renderer changed the \"deck:current\" resolution... no.\n\nLet me examine whether this behavior is a planted bug by checking if it exists in upstream AnkiDroid. In AnkiDroid 2.17, the Statistics screen has: title with deck name, dropdown to choose deck; \"deck\"/\"collection\" radio; search text. Code: `StatisticsActivity` / `StatisticsFragment`:\n- `mDeckName` shown in toolbar.\n- Selecting a deck from the picker calls `onSelectedDeck` which sets the search to `deck:\"name\"` and updates... maybe also the \"deck\" radio? I believe it does update `deckRadioButton.setChecked(true)`? Hmm.\n- `deck:current` is resolved by the backend stats using `deck_id` passed? Actually the stats backend computes `deck:current` by looking at the *collection's current deck* (`col.getCurrentDeckId()`?) — which is a collection-level setting = the last deck selected in the deck list, Spanish. Hence the mismatch.\n\nIf upstream behaves the same, the developer might say by design. But the header/query mismatch is still a bug, likely not seeded.\n\nGiven the instruction \"Signing off while bugs remain is the worst outcome\", I should report genuine issues even if unsure. But false reports could also be costly? The instructions emphasize thoroughness. The developer's confirmation is the arbiter. I'll report it as a consistency issue with wrong_value, citing the header \"French\" vs data \"Studied 4 cards\" and card counts total 5 (Spanish). Actually the report should quote the exact text showing defect. The latest observation (browser) doesn't show stats. I need to navigate to stats, reproduce, and file with element_ref/quote from that observation.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the priority: maybe there IS a chart bug I haven't noticed. Let me look at the \"Future Due\" chart with 1-month in Spanish and compare bar heights with the text. I'll do that before reporting the radio issue.\n\nActually, let me look for a more definitive chart bug: The \"Future Due\" chart for Spanish 1 month shows bars at day 0 and day 1, each height 2 (left axis). But wait, at the time we first viewed it, the summary said \"Total: 4 reviews\", \"Due tomorrow: 2 reviews\". If day 0 has 2 (learning) and day1 has 2, consistent. However, in the 1-month chart screenshot, I only saw ONE bar at the far left; maybe the two bars are at x=0 and x=1 adjacent (looked merged). Let me measure via screenshot pixel analysis: I can't run image tools, but I can view the image. The bar in the screenshot spanned from x=178 to about x=215; the x-axis tick 0 at x=178, 5 at x=295. Day width ≈ 23.4 px. A single bar of width ~1 day = 23px. The green bar looked ~37px wide — could be 2 bars each ~18px with a small gap. Plausible.\n\nWell, let me test another data case: review a French card to add data with a different deck/time, then check stats. Eh, too much.\n\nLet me check the charts' \"all history\" vs \"last 12 months\" toggle. Since all our data is today, both should be identical. Tap \"all history\" on stats and compare numbers: days studied maybe \"1 of 1\" (100%) vs \"1 of 31\". Let's check. This tests the range control.\n\nOpen stats (from browser) now: drawer → Statistics. Then select Spanish deck mode? It should be Spanish (browser Spanish)."}
