he average number of reviews per day **over the next 30 days**, counting only days with reviews\"? Hmm.\n\nHmm, could \"Daily load\" be the *number of reviews due tomorrow plus today*? In Anki, the stats show \"Daily load: 3 reviews/day\" maybe computed as the maximum over the graph period of a 7-day moving average? Not.\n\nI recall the Anki desktop Future Due stats: \"Average: 0.64 reviews/day\", \"Due tomorrow: 0 reviews\", \"Daily load: 1.20 reviews/day\". Hmm.\n\nNo need to verify; the change to daily load 3 is consistent with adding hola at 5 days: total 4 over 3 due-days... Wait, \"Daily load\" might be total/number of days from today to the last due date = 4/5 = 0.8 → 1. Not 3.\n\nHmm, let me test with the \"all\" range: for \"all\", Daily load earlier was 4 when total 4 (all within 1 day). Now with hola at 5 days, \"all\" might show Daily load = ? If Daily load = total / days spanned = 4/5 = 0.8 → 1. Let me tap \"all\" and check."}
