ion unchecked. Hmm, the stats screen state persisted from earlier? The last observed at y=113: deck focused, collection not focused. Actually this is the same statistics activity retained from before (we came back to it? no, we re-opened statistics fresh). When we opened Stats from browser, the radio was deck (default) and search deck:current. Good.\n\nNow if I choose French from the title dropdown, what happens to the radio? Earlier (fresh open) when I selected French, the radio was \"collection\" (because I had tapped collection beforehand). In a fresh session with deck radio selected, choosing French from the picker might set the radio to deck properly? Let me test now: currently deck radio selected, Spanish header. Tap title → French. Then observe header/search/radio and data.\n\nIf radio stays \"deck\" and search becomes deck:\"French\", data French → consistent. Then tap \"deck\" radio again? It wouldn't change anything. Hmm, but if the radio is already \"deck\", tapping it again sets search to deck:current → Spanish data with French header → inconsistency. The user could do that (tapping the already-selected radio). But is that a realistic bug? The radio is a search preset; tapping it when already selected would set deck:current. deck:current = the current deck from the deck list (Spanish). So the stats title should probably change to Spanish but doesn't.\n\nThe cleanest statement: After switching the statistics deck to French via the title deck picker, selecting the \"deck\" radio shows Spanish statistics while the screen title still says French. Two elements disagree. I can report with quotes \"French\" (title) and \"Studied 7 cards...\" (Spanish data). Element ref: deck_name (1) or the Today text (10).\n\nBut is this seeded? The charts renderer change wouldn't affect this. The task said sweep the stats screen; a real inconsistency counts. I'll report it — worst case the developer rejects.\n\nActually hold on, before reporting, let me verify the sequence in